+ \\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150188} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb250a0d-d536-5ce6-ab2f-0727b67dbbc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150186}] :question/id #uuid "5ece188f-13d2-531f-96e6-7621cf2eb114" :question/math-academy-id "q-64943" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$x^{2}y^{″} - 4xy^{′} + 6y =-6x + 1, x > 0$\n\nhas the complimentary function $y_{c}(x) = Ax^{2} + Bx^{3}$, find the particular solution $y_{p}(x)$ to this equation."}]}
